(1) Upon receipt of the written recommendation of the Commission for revocation, the Minister may revoke a petroleum prospecting licence or petroleum mining lease, where the applicable licensee or lessee—
    (a) fails to conduct petroleum operations in accordance with good international petroleum industry practices, the provisions of this Act and any other relevant legislation;
    (b) interrupts production for a period of over 180 consecutive days without justification or as provided for in the applicable licence, lease or approved field development plan, provided that an event of force majeure shall be an acceptable justification for interruption;
    (c) fails to fulfil the terms and conditions of the applicable licence or lease or the approved field development plan;
    (d) fails to pay to Government, as they become due, rents, royalties, taxes or other payments or production shares under this Act;
