(1) The Authority may in consultation with licensees and other stakeholders with respect to midstream petroleum liquids operations, develop a network code governing the terms of access into facilities and infrastructure used in midstream petroleum liquids operations.
(2) The network code may include the following matters—
    (a) a connection and interconnection policy, standard terms for connection to an open access petroleum liquids transportation pipeline or petroleum liquids transportation network and a statement of the connection charging methodology;
    (b) a mechanism by which users reserve capacity in facilities and infrastructure and at any time there is a greater demand for access than available capacity, a mechanism for allocating capacity between users;
